  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Epi-actephilol A may be involved in the regulation of SQ20B through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is predicted to target several entities, including DO4, which in turn targets SQ20B, and MOVP-3, which targets SQ20B as well. Additionally, Epi-actephilol A is predicted to target another entity, Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, which is itself a target of 5-(2-Hydroxyacetyl)-10H-Phenazine-1-Carboxylic Acid, which also targets SQ20B. These findings collectively indicate that Epi-actephilol A may exert its biological effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of SQ20B. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are relatively close, but the pathways are distinct, suggesting a complex regulatory mechanism. The exact nature of the interactions and their functional significance remain to be fully elucidated.",
